# ─── Supabase (cross-device visit data) ────────────────────────────────────
# Required for the QR code / visit status page to work correctly — without
# this, visits are stored per-device (localStorage) and scanning the QR from
# a different device than the one used to register will show "Visit not
# found", since that device never had the record.
#
# Leave these EMPTY to run with local (single-device) storage instead.
#
# How to get them:
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
#   2. Open  Project Settings → API
#   3. Copy the "Project URL" and the "anon public" key below
#   4. Run the SQL in  supabase/schema.sql  (SQL Editor → paste → Run)
#   5. Copy this file to  .env  and restart the dev server
#      (on Netlify/Vercel: add these as environment variables in the
#      site's build settings, then redeploy)

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://mvsennapnxvbkrrmypez.supabase.co/rest/v1/
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_FUFRH3sjGEC4t4u2vZM8dQ_4dMbFias
